Bug found and fixed. The issue was on line 14 of the original `url_utils.ts`:

```ts
for (const param of TRACKING_PARAMS) {
  if (u.searchParams.has(param)) {
    u.searchParams.delete(param);
    break;  // ← culprit: exits after the first match
  }
}
```

The `break` caused the loop to exit immediately after stripping the **first** matching tracking parameter, so any additional tracking params (e.g. `fbclid` when `utm_source` was found first) were left intact.

**Fix:** removed the `break` so the loop continues and strips every tracking param present in `TRACKING_PARAMS`.


